_in_a_headwrap_in_Quebec_City.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Woman_in_a_headwrap_in_Quebec_City.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"A passer-by in Quebec City in June 2024. Quebec City, Quebec, Canada."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2024-06-09 18:19:47"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Wilfredor\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"User:Wilfredor\">Wilfredor</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC0"}}}]},{"pageid":149883392,"title":"File:Woljeonggyo Bridge and stone steps on the bank at golden hour in Gyeongju South Korea.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Woljeonggyo_Bridge_and_stone_steps_on_the_bank_at_golden_hour_in_Gyeongju_South_Korea.jpg/960px-Woljeonggyo_Bridge_and_stone_steps_on_the_bank_at_golden_hour_in_Gyeongju_South_Korea.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Woljeonggyo_Bridge_and_stone_steps_on_the_bank_at_golden_hour_in_Gyeongju_South_Korea.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Woljeonggyo Bridge and stone steps with grass on the bank, at <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_hour_(photography)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Golden hour (photography)\">golden hour</a>, in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gyeongju\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Gyeongju\">Gyeongju</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Korea\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:South Korea\">South Korea</a>."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2024-06-09 19:01:09"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Basile_Morin\" title=\"User:Basile Morin\">Basile Morin</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":162960473,"title":"File:Woman sewing handfans.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Woman_sewing_handfans.jpg/960px-Woman_sewing_handfans.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Woman_sewing_handfans.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Handicraft is a very old profession of Bangladesh. Handmade fans are one of many types. Women in rural areas are more engaged in this profession. It makes a fan very skillfully. Its materials are mainly bast strips, colored cloth and thread. They make the hand fans very beautifully. Looks pretty nice. They make the fans and arrange them on the wall in their tin house to attract the attention of the customers. The demand for this fan is very high during the summer. Their earnings are very low, according to their performance. The demand for hand fans is decreasing due to modernity."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2024-05-04 14:56:16"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=User:Mahinur11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Mahinur11 (page does not exist)\">Mahinur11</a>, edited by <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Kaim_Amin\" title=\"User:Kaim Amin\">Kaim Amin</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":164944999,"title":"File:Wolf spider (Aglaoctenus castaneus) on web Rio Napo.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Wolf_spider_%28Aglaoctenus_castaneus%29_on_web_Rio_Napo.jpg/960px-Wolf_spider_%28Aglaoctenus_castaneus%29_on_web_Rio_Napo.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wolf_spider_(Aglaoctenus_castaneus)_on_web_Rio_Napo.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Wolf spider (<i>Aglaoctenus castaneus</i>) on web, Rio Napo, Sucumbios, Ecuador"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2025-04-19 10:16:18"},"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q54800218\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q54800218\"><span title=\"Scottish wildlife photographer\">Charles J. Sharp</span></a></bdi>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":179438665,"title":"File:Wolf Spider Guarding the Next Generation.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Wolf_Spider_Guarding_the_Next_Generation.jpg/960px-Wolf_Spider_Guarding_the_Next_Generation.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wolf_Spider_Guarding_the_Next_Generation.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"A female wolf spider (<i>Pardosa amentata</i>) with her spiderlings on her back. This photo captures a female wolf spider carrying her babies on her back. Despite her intimidating appearance, she is incredibly shy, only emerging from her hiding spot to bask in the warmth of the sun with her young. When I approached too quickly with my camera, she disappeared in an instant, retreating into the undergrowth. It took a great deal of patience before she resurfaced and settled between the leaves, allowing me to finally take this shot. It was taken in Zug and is a handheld focus stack with 30 shots."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2024-06-09 15:51:21"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Roy_Egloff\" title=\"User:Roy Egloff\">Roy Egloff</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":182449120,"title":"File:Woman kneeling next to bed of child, in an underground tunnel during the bombing of London during World War II.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Woman_kneeling_next_to_bed_of_child%2C_in_an_underground_tunnel_during_the_bombing_of_London_during_World_War_II.jpg/960px-Woman_kneeling_next_to_bed_of_child%2C_in_an_underground_tunnel_during_the_bombing_of_London_during_World_War_II.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Woman_kneeling_next_to_bed_of_child,_in_an_underground_tunnel_during_the_bombing_of_London_during_World_War_II.jpg","extmetadata":{"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"January 1945<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P571,+1945-01-00T00:00:00Z/10</div>"},"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:Toni_Frissell\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:Toni Frissell\"><span title=\"American photographer (1907–1988)\">Toni Frissell</span></a></bdi>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain"}}}]},{"pageid":183833519,"title":"File:Woman in traditional Uzbek long adras dress (Po-i-Kalyan complex, 2025 Buhara).jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Woman_in_traditional_Uzbek_long_adras_dress_%28Po-i-Kalyan_complex%2C_2025_Buhara%29.jpg/960px-Woman_in_traditional_Uzbek_long_adras_dress_%28Po-i-Kalyan_complex%2C_2025_Buhara%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Woman_in_traditional_Uzbek_long_adras_dress_(Po-i-Kalyan_complex,_2025_Buhara).jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Woman parading in traditional Uzbek long <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:Adras_(fabric)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:Adras (fabric)\">adras</a> dress in Po-i-Kalyan complex, 2025 Buhara. Adras is combination 50% wool, 50% silk. UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage Ref:  01254"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2025-09-10 09:17:12"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:PetarM\" title=\"User:PetarM\">Petar Milošević</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]}]}}